<Sequential id="writing_survey_1" title="Writing Survey 1" launchable="true">
    <Markdown id="ws1_intro">
            # Writing Survey 1
            ## Introduction

            In this survey, you will reflect on how you feel about writing and various kinds
            of writing situations. To probe how you feel, you will be presented with a series of statements, and asked to indicate whether you (a) strongly agree, (b) agree, (c) disagree, or (d) strongly disagree with that statement. Work your way through these statements, picking the answer that seems to match your own experience and feelings best. There are quite a few statements to get through, so don't take too much time on any single statement. At the end, we will give you a computer-generated summary of your answers.
    </Markdown>
    <Vertical id="ws1_Step_1" title="Survey Questions 1-5">
        <Markdown>
            ## Questions 1-5
            Indicate how strongly you agree or disagree with the following statements.
        </Markdown>
        <TabularMCQ id="ws1_affect_1">
          cols: Strongly Agree, Agree, Disagree, Strongly Disagree
          rows: Writing is a skill I want to get better at.,It is frustrating to have to write about a subject that I did not choose.,Writing is usually boring for me.,I worry that other people will criticize my writing.,I like to write outside of school.
        </TabularMCQ>
        <Markdown id="ws1_directions">
          Select one option for each row. Your selections are automatically saved.
        </Markdown>
      </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="ws1_Step_2" title="Survey Questions 6-10">
        <Markdown>
            ## Questions 6-10
            Indicate how strongly you agree or disagree with the following statements.
        </Markdown>
        <TabularMCQ id="ws1_affect_2">
          cols: Strongly Agree, Agree, Disagree, Strongly Disagree
          rows: It upsets me when I get low grades on a writing assignment.,I am too impatient to spend a lot of time writing.,I get so involved in my writing that I often lose track of time.,Writing helps me learn.,I feel it is important to know how to write well.
        </TabularMCQ>
        <Markdown id="ws1_directions">
          Select one option for each row. Your selections are automatically saved.
        </Markdown>
    </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="ws1_Step_3" title="Survey Questions 11-15">
        <Markdown>
            ## Questions 11-15
            Indicate how strongly you agree or disagree with the following statements.
        </Markdown>
        <TabularMCQ id="ws1_affect_3">
          cols: Strongly Agree, Agree, Disagree, Strongly Disagree
          rows: I prefer to avoid writing when it isn't required.,I like getting lots of shares or likes on social media when I post something I have written.,There are some subjects that I really enjoy writing about.,I dislike writing.,I find it difficult to communicate my ideas through writing.
        </TabularMCQ>
        <Markdown id="ws1_directions">
          Select one option for each row. Your selections are automatically saved.
        </Markdown>
    </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="ws1_Step_4" title="Survey Questions 16-20">
        <Markdown>
            ## Questions 16-20
            Indicate how strongly you agree or disagree with the following statements.
        </Markdown>
        <TabularMCQ id="ws1_affect_4">
          cols: Strongly Agree, Agree, Disagree, Strongly Disagree
          rows: I like it when people compliment my writing skills.,I feel confident when I am writing.,It's important that I get a good grade on a writing assignment.,When I write I create content that I can be proud of.,Writing feels really hard.
        </TabularMCQ>
        <Markdown id="ws1_directions">
          Select one option for each row. Your selections are automatically saved.
        </Markdown>
    </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="ws1_Step_5" title="Survey Questions 21-26">
        <Markdown>
            ## Questions 21-26
            Indicate how strongly you agree or disagree with the following statements.
        </Markdown>
        <TabularMCQ id="ws1_affect_5">
          cols: Strongly Agree, Agree, Disagree, Strongly Disagree
          rows: I usually enjoy writing in school.,I find writing interesting.,I enjoy writing most when I get to decide what to write about.,I understand things better when I write about them.,There are some kinds of writing that I really like.,I like it when I can focus and my writing flows.
        </TabularMCQ>
        <Markdown id="ws1_directions">
          Select one option for each row. Your selections are automatically saved.
        </Markdown>
    </Vertical>
    <Vertical id="ws1_Step_6">
           <ActionButton label="Analyze my feelings about writing">
               <LLMAction target="ws1_response_summary_6">
                  BACKGROUND INFORMATION:
                   For the survey pages that ask about student feelings about writing,
                   Our column headers are:
                         Strongly Agree (corresponding to 0),
                         Agree (corresponding to 1),
                         Disagree (corresponding to 2),
                         Strongly Disagree (corresponding to 3),

                   Our row headers are:
                   Writing is a skill I want to get better at.
                   It is frustrating to have to write about a subject that I did not choose.
                   Writing is usually boring for me.
                   I worry that other people will criticize my writing.
                   I like to write outside of school.
                   It upsets me when I get low grades on a writing assignment.
                   I am too impatient to spend a lot of time writing.
                   I get so involved in my writing that I often lose track of time.
                   Writing helps me learn.
                   I feel it is important to know how to write well.
                   I prefer to avoid writing when it isn't required.
                   I like getting lots of shares or likes on social media when I post something I have written.
                   There are some subjects that I really enjoy writing about.
                   I dislike writing.
                   I find it difficult to communicate my ideas through writing.
                   I like it when people compliment my writing skills.
                   I feel confident when I am writing.
                   It's important that I get a good grade on a writing assignment.
                   When I write I create content that I can be proud of.
                   Writing feels really hard.
                   I usually enjoy writing in school.
                   I find writing interesting.
                   I enjoy writing most when I get to decide what to write about.
                   I understand things better when I write about them.\
                   There are some kinds of writing that I really like.
                   I like it when I can focus and my writing flows.

                   Our data is:
                   <Ref id="ws1_ref6" target="ws1_affect_1" />
                   <Ref id="ws1_ref7" target="ws1_affect_2" />
                   <Ref id="ws1_ref8" target="ws1_affect_3" />
                   <Ref id="ws1_ref9" target="ws1_affect_4" />
                   <Ref id="ws1_ref10" target="ws1_affect_5" />

                  This data can be interpreted by mapping each number onto the column header it corresponds
                  to and using the row headers to indicate the level of agreement the student selected for each statement.

                  These statements can be grouped into the following factors:

                  Factor 1 (Difficulty/Interest).

                  Agreement with the following statements indicates the student feels that
                  writing is boring and difficult:
                  I dislike writing.
                  It is frustrating to write about a subject that I did not choose.
                  Writing is usually boring for me.
                  I find it difficult to communicate my ideas through writing.
                  I prefer to avoid writing when it isn't required.
                  Writing feels really hard.

                  Disagreement with the following statements indicates the student feels
                  that writing is boring and difficult:
                  I find writing interesting.
                  I understand things better when I write about them.

                  Factor 2 (Agency)
                  Agreement with the following statements indicates the student feels
                  a sense of control and agency in the writing process:
                  There are some subjects I really enjoy writing about.
                  I like it when I can focus and my writing flows.
                  There are some kinds of writing that I really like.
                  I enjoy writing most when I get to decide what to write about.
                  I like it when people compliment my writing skills.
                  It's important that I get a good grade on a writing assignment.
                  It upsets me when I get low grades on a writing assignment.

                  Factor 3 (Self-efficacy)
                  Agreement with the following statements indicates that the student
                  has a high degree of confidence in his/her writing skills:
                  I like getting lots of shares or likes on social media.
                  I get so involved in my writing that I often lose track of time.
                  I feel confident in my writing.
                  I usually enjoy writing in school.
                  When I write, I create content that I can be proud of.
                  I like to write outside of school.

                  Disagreement with the following statement also suggests a high
                  degree of writing self-confidence:
                  I am too impatient to spend a lot of time writing.

                  Factor 4 (Intrinsic value)
                  Agreement with the following statements indicates that the student believes
                  that writing has high intrinsic value as a skill he/she needs to learn:
                  Writing helps me learn.
                  I feel it is important to know how to write well.
                  Writing is a skill I want to get better at.
                  I worry that other people will criticize my writing.

                  DIRECTIONS:
                   If any of the student's response data is blank, say so and stop; otherwise,
                   using the information from the data interpretation, and addressing the
                   student as "you", write a numbered, bulleted list that describes the student's
                   attitudes towards writing in terms of these four factors. Do not include
                   the phrases "Factor 1", "Factor 2", "Factor 3" or "Factor 4" in your response.
           </LLMAction>
          </ActionButton>
        <LLMFeedback id="ws1_response_summary_6" />
    </Vertical>
